    edge_case tests/test_bst.py:test_inorder_returns_fresh_list: The test mutates the returned list but never checks that the returned object is not shared with internal state beyond the value list; it also asserts identity via 't.inorder() is not t.inorder()' which is trivially true for any implementation returning a new list and does not verify no aliasing of internal storage.
    edge_case bst.py:BinarySearchTree._size: _size is maintained but never exposed or tested; it is dead state that could drift if later tasks (delete, duplicates) touch insert paths without updating it.
    edge_case bst.py:BinarySearchTree.insert (mixed types): Values are assumed mutually comparable but nothing enforces it; inserting 1 then 'a' raises TypeError midway through the descent, and the tree is unchanged only because the failing comparison happens before assignment. This is good but untested.
    edge_case tests/test_bst.py:test_all_permutations_of_small_set: Only covers 4 distinct values; no coverage for empty-tree-then-insert-duplicate-of-root or inserting the root value again on a single-node tree.
