    """Binary Search Tree implementation (standard library only).               
                                                                                
    Requirements on values: they must form a total order (any two values must be
    comparable with ``<`` and exactly one of ``a < b``, ``a == b``, ``b < a``   
    must                                                                        
    hold). Values that are not equal to themselves (NaN, including              
    ``decimal.Decimal('NaN')`` and signalling NaNs) are rejected with           
    ``ValueError``                                                              
    on insert and are never found by search, because they would break the       
    ordering                                                                    
    invariant.                                                                  
                                                                                
    Duplicates (values equal under ``<``) are ignored. Insert, search and       
    inorder                                                                     
    traversal are iterative, so deep trees do not hit the recursion limit.      
                                                                                
    Exception contract:                                                         
    - insert raises ValueError for NaN-like values and TypeError for values that
      are not comparable with stored values; the tree is unchanged in both      
    cases.                                                                      
